ctions from provisional mappings.", :id "M-aif-wiring#6dc6843d9c37"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 181, :text "- [ ] Named AIF quantities carry real-or-analogical grounding metadata checked by a failing-test control.", :id "M-aif-wiring#248166606d96"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 182, :text "- [ ] The AIF structure-learning criterion records morphogenesis events and enforces the joint free-energy and expected-free-energy improvement gate.", :id "M-aif-wiring#84fad92a44e4"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 183, :text "- [ ] A consent-gated WM executor observes action consequences and feeds them into belief updates and policy-precision learning.", :id "M-aif-wiring#f0687b76b834"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 184, :text "- [ ] A hierarchical generative-model design specifies its levels and cross-level belief propagation.", :id "M-aif-wiring#c89c11cd2747"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 4, :text "**Status:** OPEN — **IDENTIFY** (new mission; successor home for the R14–R18 gaps surfaced by the now-closed M-wm-policies). *Name provisional — Joe may rename.*", :id "M-aif-wiring#af3fd67e1975"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 69, :text "### Open questions (honest unknowns for IDENTIFY)", :id "M-aif-wiring#a3aa96633993"} {:kind :open-section-item, :line 71, :text "- **Rendering R15 and R18 together.** R15 wants the map *nested*; R18 wants every node *colored* real/analogical. What single representation carries both without becoming unreadable?", :id "M-aif-wiring#d121c1137243"} {:kind :open-section-item, :line 72, :text "- **New node shapes for what Friston's figure omits.** R8/R9/R10 (runs / logs / validates), R11 (one-of-many), R17 (rewrites itself) have no canonical brain slot. Do they sit *on* the brain, or in a surrounding apparatus frame around it?", :id "M-aif-wiring#ed97fae7feba"} {:kind :open-section-item, :line 73, :text "- **Authoritativeness.** Which R maps to which Friston term — and whether an **R19+** is missing — rests on the **first-pass** AIF∩morphogenesis component list (~10/25 verified before the run died; see [[E-deep-research-hardening]]). The diagram must mark first-pass vs verified mappings; a full adversarial research round (E-aif2-partB §4) hardens it.", :id "M-aif-wiring#9430ceb5fc45"} {:kind :open-section-item, :line 74, :text "- **Tooling + \"no fabricated structure.\"** Whatever draws it (Graphviz / SVG-over-the-brain-image / a live futon surface), the wiring must reflect **real code edges** — which namespace actually calls which — not an idealized textbook loop. The M-wm-policies regulator lesson (\"don't fabricate dynamics\") applies to diagrams too: a wiring diagram that shows connections the code doesn't have is fiction.", :id "M-aif-wiring#b28d2a656b33"}], :status-line "OPEN — **IDENTIFY** (new mission; successor home for the R14–R18 gaps surfaced by the now-closed M-wm-policies). *Name provisional — Joe may rename.*", :operator-gate-lines []} {:path "/home/joe/code/futon7/holes/M-cold-chain.md", :open-hole-count 8, :status-class :open, :source {:path "/home/joe/code/futon7/holes/M-cold-chain.md", :sha256 "455b1b6c7e53354b98296aa86915dc6797fafb3c4367579a45505ae0f00ebd27"}, :title "M-cold-chain — ground the four cold-* stars as one ladder", :requisition {:absent :no-requisition}, :operator-gated? false, :id "M-cold-chain", :kind :mission, :open-holes [{:kind :unchecked-task, :line 175, :text "- [ ] A real cold EOI is staged with target, scan provenance, and interest-territory match recorded.", :id "M-cold-chain#8f0cc23f5a66"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 176, :text "- [ ] The send-gate surface exists and Joe has reviewed it.", :id "M-cold-chain#4dea324e812a"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 177, :text "- [ ] A kit-intake demonstration turns an `:outreach-sent` event into typed evidence and observable response/conversion rungs.", :id "M-cold-chain#3eea5cfad448"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 178, :text "- [ ] Each `cold-*` star references this mission and flips only from its operator-witnessed typed rec