d be able to do", :requisition {:absent :no-requisition}, :operator-gated? false, :id "M-wm-capability-claim", :kind :mission, :open-holes [{:kind :unchecked-task, :line 145, :text "- [ ] An append-only L1 ledger records the operator's verdict at recommendation time and records an endorse-rate threshold fixed before the first window closes.", :id "M-wm-capability-claim#d66893a5c7aa"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 146, :text "- [ ] One complete L1 window reports the WM's endorse rate whether it meets the preregistered threshold or not.", :id "M-wm-capability-claim#d683d3cb0227"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 147, :text "- [ ] Two comparable L1 windows exist and report whether endorse rate rose, stayed flat, or declined as run history accumulated.", :id "M-wm-capability-claim#090c9cf49cda"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 148, :text "- [ ] A written L3 adjudication design names an outcome authority independent of the operator who disagreed with the recommendation.", :id "M-wm-capability-claim#391a0c7728e5"}], :status-line "OPEN — SPEC. Prerequisite for M-aif-stack S2.", :operator-gate-lines []} {:path "/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-wm-wiring.md", :open-hole-count 16, :status-class :open, :source {:path "/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-wm-wiring.md", :sha256 "2645b304ac1c3cfe6167038519fadfd43afd2330bb4036fa56220573475b1343"}, :title "Mission: M-wm-wiring", :requisition {:absent :no-requisition}, :operator-gated? false, :id "M-wm-wiring", :kind :mission, :open-holes [{:kind :unchecked-task, :line 10, :text "- [ ] Every wiring row's tripwire and named test box pass against the committed map.", :id "M-wm-wiring#acd2d4bb185b"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 11, :text "- [ ] The map's `:expected-findings` contains only the two standing findings named by the mission.", :id "M-wm-wiring#a45bb57880d5"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 12, :text "- [ ] N0 holds when a flight run's closure includes the wired files.", :id "M-wm-wiring#d1dc0b0eb999"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 13, :text "- [ ] The first flight's record is reviewed and accepted whether the flight succeeds or fails.", :id "M-wm-wiring#480b799fea4d"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 14, :text "- [ ] The DOCUMENT page contains the mission annotations and lifecycle evidence rather than reporting them absent.", :id "M-wm-wiring#19dcac8b77e3"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 300, :text "| process | dangling wire, unowned field, unreachable state | the diagramprover run, registered (test-registry-b9f1a1a2 at fbb094f3): `written-never-read`, `read-never-written`, `multiply-written`, `conformance` under `{:heuristic? true}` at var grain, the trace checks, the `:not-built` absence checks, N0's load-closure check; detect-level. Priced hole: by-construction grade is not reachable here; revisit trigger: when M-diagramprover's WS-D line lands, or when a second written-but-not-wired finding survives a wiring commit |", :id "M-wm-wiring#0f4616e28b19"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 3, :text "**Status:** OPEN — HEAD, IDENTIFY, MAP, DERIVE, ARGUE met (Joe's read, 2026-09-25 ~23:55Z: \"it looks good to me\"); VERIFY entered (the wiring as a whole, by the diagramprover run over the machine's map); INSTANTIATE drafted: the overall wiring first, then the missing parts and hops.", :id "M-wm-wiring#0264b1f49908"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 92, :text "**The ruling.** Components AND wires are verified before any flight runs again. The map is the specification of the remaining work, not a record of it. A flight is a test of the whole and stops at its first defect, so it bounds nothing about what remains (the \"each one typed and fixed\" correction, 2026-09-26); verification of each wire does.", :id "M-wm-wiring#aba81643a2e0"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 107, :text "4. **The hand-offs**: WM-HANDOFFS-D's H1-H7, one packet each, and the carriers as boxes. WM-HANDOFF-H2-I DONE (futon3c b44b63ab map + fixture + map test + lane table, 8dc61b63 figures and matrix, 73e335e0 ledger; claude-10, ~12:29Z; claude-8: record check holds, warrants fd1a469a map, 392eb1ce replay, 3a640366 projection, 31699c43 ledger 3/217; figures published). THE 3→4 BOUNDARY IS CROSSED by six keys of the interpretation store: the `reading` ns is `futon2.aif.mission-reading`; every publish function reads `<store>/<target>.edn`, assocs its key, writes back atomically; one writer and one reader per key, all twelve sites in that file: `:criteria` `:coverage` `:locators` `:locator-questions` `:locator-declines` `:constraints-read` (the store's own key, not `:constraints`), writers `publish-*!`/`record-locator-decline!` in lane 3, readers `published-*` in lane 4 (their returns become the wants `run!` computes with `click-wants` just before `ask-fn`, `flight.clj:325-335`). `source-wants` is a `defmulti`, which the prover's var-grain site cannot see past the docstring, so the read-back functions are the boxed readers and its calls are positional (map comment). Findings 218 → 235 (17 standing occurrences with notes); matrix 98 → 104, boundary 2→3 from 0 to 6 wires; islands now lanes 5 and 6 only; strip 15 fields cross steps, 2 of 11 steps untouched; ledger 0/2/102 of 104; fixture 34/23/69/139, all twelve boxes in the dead components since no test box reads a store key. One slip caught before any commit: an annotation script crash left H1's stale entries on the working map; restored from git and redone. WM-HANDOFF-H3-I DONE (futon3c 5927020d map + fixture + map test + lane table, 5d71e012 figures and matrix, 2d4eeeb6 ledger; claude-10, ~12:35Z; claude-8: record check holds, warrants 80da7955 map, 4305f517 replay, 2abd8d5b projection, d8f36f5a ledger 3/227; figures published). `flight/click-wants` (lane 4) is the one writer of `:wants` and `:universe`; `flight/judge-opts` (lane 10) reads them and re-emits them under the click's `:flight` (standing occurrences); futon3c `handle-wm-click-start` (`:click-start`) reads the posted `:wants`; `war_machine/flight-assembly-input` (`:tick-flight-assembly`, lane 5, called by `judge` with `(:flight judge-opts)`) reads `:wants` `:locators` `:universe` and writes them into the assembly's `:sources`; `cascade_problems/assemble-one` then reads `[:wants target]` for the problem's `:want`, so C reaches the problem THERE, and that hop is not declared (the sources map has other writers; its own packet, H8). `:locators` is NOT declared on this carrier: its one writer is already H2's store entry and the prover has no per-record scope (three standing occurrences). THE BOUNDARY CROSSED IS 4→5 (ask → construction), not 7→8: in the lane table the tick's own steps are lanes 5, 6, 7a, 7b, and the receiver builds the input construction works over. 5→6 and 6→7a light up only because `:wants` has readers in lane 10, and the strip counts a field at every boundary between writer and furthest reader; only 4→5 has a reader at the step itself. Islands: lane 6 (Rates) only. Findings 235 → 248 (13 standing with notes); matrix 104 → 109 (five wires from `click-wants`); ledger 0/2/107 of 109; strip 17 fields cross steps, 1 of 11 steps untouched; fixture 35/23/72/145. futon2 pin unchanged. WM-HANDOFF-H4-I DONE (futon3c dd0c145f, dcd55083, 480bd170; claude-10, ~12:46Z; claude-8: record check holds, warrants 1fe7ffc1 map, 006730a8 replay, 51f8de0e projection, eb75083e ledger 3/231, figures published): the one writer of `:interpretations` is `merge-published` (`want_interpretation.clj:473`, box `:ask-merge-published`, lane 4), which reads the store back into the sources; `:272` is a trial assembly inside `validate-response` that never leaves it; neither is a publish, so the field does not split. Readers in lane 5: `:construction-assemble-one` (`[:interpretations target]`) and `:construction-construct` (destructured, via `constructed-from-interpretations`, not boxed). `target-view` NOT boxed: it calls `merge-published` and its form has no `:interpretations`; it carries `:universe`, and the `:universes` writer is `flight-assembly-input`, so H5's writer changes. `:r0-enact-step` reads the store's `:patterns` under an option built by `run-flight!`, not this key: standing. 4→5 now `interpretations universe wants`, both `:interpretations` readers at the step; no later lane reads it; island still lane 6 only. Findings 248 → 263 (3 to-do, one of them `:wants` at `assemble-one`, H8's); matrix 109 → 111 (the three new boxes their own component); ledger 0/2/109; fixture 36/23/75/148, new input `:world/ask-merge-published`. WM-HANDOFF-H5-I DONE (futon3c 3597ba36, 6b084cb8, a716e024; claude-10, ~12:52Z; claude-8: record check holds, warrants 9c2d3f50 map, 8911026a replay, d7ce560d projection, 0d1f4494 ledger 3/233): `:universes` from `:tick-flight-assembly` (`(update-in [:sources :universes target] merge (:universe flight))`) to `:construction-assemble-one` (`[:universes target]` as the problem's `:facts`, passed positionally to `constructed-from-interpretations`); both lane 5, no boundary change; `construct` does not read it. 264 findings (3 to-do), 112 wires, ledger 0/2/110, fixture 36/23/75/149. H4 CORRECTED where it stands: the sources' `:interpretations`/`:wants`/`:universes` are also written in `judge` (war_machine ~7222) by `cascade_sources/load-declared` (`:285`) and `mission_hole_wants/merge-into-sources` (`:158`) before `flight-assembly-input`, whose merge runs last (a token the flight located wins). H8 HELD: the sources' `:wants` has those writers too, and `:wants` already has the click's declared writer; the prover refuses two writers per field name (`wiring.clj:77-81`). claude-8: a prover schema change, per-record scope, dispatched to claude-2 (WM-PROVER-RECORD-SCOPE-I); WM-HANDOFF-H6-I DONE (futon3c e930fd49, 0d7042e8, d4111d55; claude-10, ~13:00Z; claude-8: record check holds, warrants 6679f693 map, 5fe9cf61 replay, 45e75675 projection, 806cdbf0 ledger 3/241; figures published): `:construction-receipt` written once by `construct` (carried on by `constructed-from-interpretations`, which adds `:unknown