bit store (`:cascade-habit-path`) as E's source at selection once row 7 lands, its tripwire in row 7's test. Tripwires: 10 in place (the extractor control f4576030; served-by-reading b21deaa0; nf-4/nb-4 21b3bb44; grain-gate 9bb4d15f; enactment-habit 2730f868; target-field 4ef4b04b; the W_c check 1757d974; the diagramprover control f24589cc; the map's test 5cdd0298; row 11's check with no warrant recorded this sitting, `:warrant nil` with a note), 11 to write, each named with its row's test-box namespace from the map so the matrix and the map change in the same commit. Not yet in the matrix: the loop-closure boxes, which come with the next map commit (WM-MAP-I2). Earlier plan, superseded: (claude-10, ~21:50Z: one matrix row per inventory row, each tripwire beside that row's test box, so the two stay in step). Preserve: nf-4 and nb-4; the extractor control; the diagramprover control reports; row 6's numbers pinned unchanged with `:measurement :absent` on every class. Adapt: row 4, the chain case exactly equal to the list kernel as the row-4 tripwire; row 1, the no-data case reducing to E alone. Drop: the legacy habit store as E's source, listed once row 7 makes selection read the fold. A Capability Preservation Matrix per row: *preserve* (rows whose change must leave existing behaviour byte-identical, with the tripwire already in place: the all-finite constructor output nf-4/nb-4 pinned to fixtures; the M-futon-seams extractor control; the diagramprover control reports; row 6's numbers unchanged today), *adapt* (row 4: G changes on non-chain containment, tripwire = the chain case equal to the list kernel exactly, recorded against Lean 69c2; row 1: selection reads the fold and the eligible field, tripwire = the no-data case reduces to E alone), *drop* (none known; the legacy habit store as E's source once selection reads the fold, to be listed if so).", :id "M-wm-wiring#a9cdcbb901d2"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 256, :text "- Trace in the map: N-run and the `:traces` field (next map commit); load-closure resolution (N0) as its precondition.", :id "M-wm-wiring#6c0dc1bbe15e"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 263, :text "**Why this design and not another.** The gap is that every component exists and nothing calls it, and that earlier rounds spent their time on refusals whose contracts were never specified. The design answers both with one object: a map that declares, per component, which record fields it reads and writes, checked against the real source by a checker that already exists, with its remaining findings declared exactly. Wiring then has one meaning, a declared read or write that the code now performs, and one test, the finding leaving the map in the same commit as the code. Red tape has one meaning too: a refusal on the register without a case, and the register is complete for the path a first flight takes up to the click (flight and tick); a flight that enacts reaches a chosen action, and the post-choice register (claude-3, on first reach) precedes the first enacting flight (owner's correction, ~23:35Z). Nothing in the design is a new contract; every field it names is one PROOF-2a's clauses already require on the record.", :id "M-wm-wiring#03a06c278eb9"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 328, :text "| 6 | 8 | DONE (claude-10; futon2 b44998f6 the change and 058c995e a key rename, warrant test-registry-b70a6a25, `futon2.aif.target-field-overlap-test` 3/10; target-field-test 12/96; futon3c 2784fcba map and matrix, warrant test-registry-c6d0ca11, map test 6/19; ct-projection-test 10/30; claude-8: record check holds on all three, ran the new namespace once in futon2's own JVM, green, the map at 15). `with-pair-overlap` gives, for an entry with a constructed candidate, one result per other feasible target: `{:comparable true}` when the candidate moves no token in that target's universe, `{:incommensurable {:shared-tokens [...]}}` naming the tokens it moves (compare-g's shape), `{:absent :no-universe}` when the other target records none; an entry with no constructed candidate records `{:absent :no-constructed-candidate}`, never `{}`. Tests: shared token → incommensurable named; disjoint → comparable; the relation is not symmetric; missing universe and missing candidate each typed, no `{}` anywhere; the pinned live read at 7bd17dfb gives 343 of 343 absent; the field's other keys byte-identical to a fixture from 42b5abdc; mutation (no token ever shared) fails. THE MAP CAUGHT A NAMING COLLISION: the entry's key had been `:candidate`, which on the map is the selection law's candidate id, so the checker flagged it and 058c995e renames it `:constructed-candidate` (nothing reads it yet). Map re-pinned to 058c995e, `r8-overlap`'s site moved to `with-pair-overlap`, both row-8 findings gone, one standing added (the test's fixture entries carry `:next-step`), 16 → 15 (8 to-do, 7 standing); matrix row 8 in place, totals 18 in place / 8 to write |", :id "M-wm-wiring#9d476b6cf94f"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 330, :text "| 8 | 7 (read side), the DROP | HELD by the owner, then decided (claude-10 ~19:50Z; claude-8 ~20:00Z). The drop is implemented as a patch, futon2 418bce68 `proof2/pending/step8-selection-reads-fold.patch` (the shared tree at HEAD, claude-8 confirmed clean): `select-action-cascades` takes E from `opts :enactment-fold` (the fold's state) through a new `cascade-habit-store/attach-state`, same masses and fallback, no store read; uniform E with no fold; the selection law records `:e-source {:source :enactment-fold :records n :samples s :uniform bool}` and the habit provenance names `:enactment-fold`; `:cascade-habit-path` is no longer read. Drop line: \"the legacy habit store (`:cascade-habit-path`, `data/cascade-prior.edn`, filled by the legacy selection writer and the runner's close rule without W_c) is no longer read at selection; E comes from the enactment fold. The store stays on disk as history.\" Its 21 samples (H-E-D): 17 by the legacy selection writer, 4 by the close rule,