context; the horizon 4 from `T-repair-occ-444fb018.edn` (the target's own computed horizon would be 6). WHY UNTYPED: `explicit-failure-kind` reads `:failure-kind`/`:outcome`; every joint-decision throw types under `:kind` (`war_machine.clj:6237,6240,6301,6323,6437,6624`; others use `:constructor/refusal`, `ticket-queue/validate!`, the gate's `:error`/`:reason`); the ex-data reached only the repair finding; a throw writes neither a decision nor the `:no-selection` sorry cell, so `abstention-carrier` took its nil branch. FIX (runner side, per register §D2.2's class T: \"the abstention carrier records it, the flight's click-summary reads it\"; not the throw sites, which would still charge a machine repair, nor the gate's closed `allowed-refusal-kinds`): the selection catch writes `:judge-refusal {:kind :target :data}` on the sorry cell and closes without a repair obligation; `abstention-carrier` gains the `{:status :abstained :targets […]}` branch; `record-summary` already lifts it onto the click entry. WM-CLICK-REFUSAL-I belled with the bad case, the live pin from the repair finding, and an untyped control. Register: `:class-unknown-no-scalar-g` needs a T row in §D2.2 (claude-3, D8). **THE DEFINITION QUESTION FOR JOE (Clause T): a machine-read target has no facet-corpus relation row by construction, so what gives a flight target its relation?** The options as the code stands: (a) a relation row authored per target in `commit-facets-v1.json` (the receipt owner's; nine exist); (b) a machine reading of the relation from the mission text at click time, with a cued receipt, on the same footing as criteria and constraints (the compute-on-the-fly rule); (c) a class other than `:unknown` for a target with no row, which is a value standing in for an absence and is refused by the typed-absence rule. Horizon and beta are a lesser question: scoring a flight target in the family's declared values or its own computed ones costs nothing new either way; only the relation decides whet