chine-aif-last-mile", :kind :mission, :open-holes [{:kind :unchecked-task, :line 393, :text "- [ ] A coordinated WM/VSATARCS observation record compares the two sides' cycle traces and records drift magnitude and status agreement.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#f741c9baccb6"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 394, :text "- [ ] `:address-sorry` candidates receive per-target G discrimination, with a focused test showing distinct targets no longer tie solely by action class.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#19d9051ea77a"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 395, :text "- [ ] Each remaining open entry in `futon2/data/sorrys.edn` is closed, reclassified with evidence, or retained with an explicit prototyping-forward rationale.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#e6d5abdd0579"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 396, :text "- [ ] The WM completeness ledger records the disposition of the deeper R12 directions and the VSATARCS-side atom-namespace decision.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#bfb870ab1ddc"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 66, :text "**Landed 2026-05-21 (claude-9):** Joe authorized the install. `crontab -l` now carries two entries: `:wm-scheduled` at `0 * * * *` (matching the recommendation; log path moved to `/home/joe/code/futon2/logs/wm-scheduled.log` for naming consistency with the new `:wm-outer-loop` log) plus `:wm-outer-loop` at `0 4 * * *` (the §2.I take-up — see below). First cron-shell smoke ran successfully; today's trace file `wm-trace-2026-05-21.edn` has the cron-emitted record (decision `:address-sorry :target :sorry/wm-aif-substrate-addressability G=-4.5461`). R10 transitions from `:scheduled-execution-ready` to `:scheduled-execution-running`. Canonical cron registry now at `/home/joe/code/futon0/data/cron-jobs.edn` mirrored as Arxana hyperedge `arxana/index/cron-jobs` so future cron additions stay legible.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#bee05c06ad13"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 72, :text "- **1 `:kind :meta`** — `:sorry/wm-aif-substrate-addressability` (the meta-sorry registering the substrate-addressability question itself; raised 2026-05-17). Partially answered by the WM apparatus existing AT ALL but the deeper question — should substrate-2 / stack-annotations.edn / M-INC events become the canonical addressable substrate for sorries — remains open.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#dd6ae99e5447"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 73, :text "- **1 `:kind :prototyping-forward`** — `:sorry/r3d-per-entity-attribution`. **Half-closed** by v0.16 multi-channel sign-aggregation (the multi-channel limitation); the per-entity-attribution half (currently all entities get the same global update) remains open until real per-entity event streams arrive (M-INC step (b)).", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#871e8ba0072f"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 74, :text "- **10 `:kind :prototyping-forward`** — `:sorry/r3a-likelihood-<channel>` for each of the 10 observation channels lacking R3a likelihood. Candidates: `:loop-health`, `:support-coverage`, `:attack-coverage`, `:stack-pct`, `:consulting-pct`, `:portfolio-pct`, `:mathematics-pct`, `:coupling-density`, `:ticks-firing-ratio`, `:depositing-signal`. Per the rationale on each: some may turn out to be belief-independent by design (commit-percentages, externally-measured ratios) and warrant reclassification to `:n-a-by-design` — that's a structural-review move per sorry, not a bulk decision.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#23a6a29e43c4"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 76, :text "**Verified 2026-05-20:** the live registry still matches this count and categorisation exactly: 12 open entries total = 1 `:meta`, 1 `:prototyping-forward` (`:sorry/r3d-per-entity-attribution` with partial-closure note from v0.16), and 10 channel-coverage `:prototyping-forward` entries.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#73fd5af1405e"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 109, :text "Surfaced 2026-05-20 by VSATARCS v0.5.13's Q2 top-K chrome: under v0.16 EFE composition, the top-3 ranked `:address-sorry` candidates all tie at G=-4.208 against different `:sorry/...` targets. Verdict: **structural, not a bug**. `forward-model/predict-effects :address-sorry` returns target-invariant observation delta (line 66: `{:sorry-count-norm -0.1 :mission-health +0.02}` regardless of target); `sorry-enumerator-proposer` doesn't add `:intrinsic-value` to the candidates; so all `:address-sorry` actions compute to identical G-total. The apparatus correctly surfaces \"addressing A sorry is high-value\" but doesn't discriminate among sorry targets in the EFE.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#ea987efd250c"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 155, :text "- The WM is a SINGLE observer at strategic scope (the futon stack's mission/sorry/observation surface).", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#a369eee1107b"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 211, :text "**Subtle observation discovered during INSTANTIATE:** the inner loop only emits `:learn-action-class :target-class :address-sorry` when `:address-sorry` has no addressable substrate (when `can-propose?` returns false). After §2.E v0.18 + v0.19 closed and the substrate adapters started returning true, `:address-sorry` stopped being a gap-class — the WM picks concrete `:address-sorry :target ...` actions directly. So the R12 inference for `:address-sorry` has no input under the current bootstrap-proposer semantics; the Beta posterior will sit at the prior even with cron running for weeks. **This is an interesting structural finding, not a bug.** If we want `:address-sorry` to also move under R12 inference, a separate design move is needed — e.g., always emit `:learn-action-class :intrinsic-value-credit-rating` recommendations alongside concrete `:address-sorry` actions (credit for class-level priority, not for substrate gap). Worth surfacing to a later session as a §2.J candidate; logged in M-the-futon-stack's 2026-05-21 checkpoint append.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#6bac164133bc"} {:kind :work-marker, :line 220, :text "- **§2.E.1 per-target G-discrimination for `:address-sorry`**: still open. The R12 narrow take-up doesn't break the G=-4.208 tie among `:sorry/...` targets that VSATARCS v0.5.13's Q2 chrome surfaced — that's a per-target intrinsic-value or per-target `predict-effects` move, distinct from per-class intrinsic-value.", :id "M-war-machine-aif-last-mile#6ecc88716ced"}], :status-line "OPEN — Open; carry-over from M-war-machine-aif-completion's v0.16 close. Salt-down for a new REPL-bound agent picking up from where this session paused.", :operator-gate-lines []} {:path "/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-codex-sorry-loop.md", :open-hole-count 5, :status-class :open, :source {:path "/home/joe/code/futon3c/holes/missions/M-codex-sorry-loop.md", :sha256 "54683435741dbbd3cb2bf3a89c8fa723832ef26878d1eff16875da9ade0c7a3d"}, :title "M-codex-sorry-loop — the learning loop on a second runner and a second work class", :requisition {:absent :no-requisition}, :operator-gated? false, :id "M-codex-sorry-loop", :kind :mission, :open-holes [{:kind :unchecked-task, :line 14, :text "- [ ] The APM corpus has no transitive `sorryAx` in any problem proof.", :id "M-codex-sorry-loop#e9ae94abc6d4"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 15, :text "- [ ] Every formal problem statement has a reviewed faithfulness audit against its original exam text.", :id "M-codex-sorry-loop#f96e166cb615"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 16, :text "- [ ] The full provenance ledger publishes interventions and misdispatches alongside successful runs.", :id "M-codex-sorry-loop#ba1c2633b04c"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 17, :text "- [ ] A fresh held-out BPM problem completes the untouched API-driven loop without mining contamination.", :id "M-codex-sorry-loop#dbf53da28ce2"} {:kind :unchecked-task, :line 18, :text "- [ ] The continuous meters record the Codex lane's receipts and mined-memory connectivity.", :id "M-codex-sorry-loop#3b112cab3257"}], :status-line "OPEN — **CHARTERED at Joe's direction** (this conversation: \"produce a", :operator-gate-lines []} {:path "/home/joe