 :unchecked-task, :line 22, :text "- [ ] `argument_v9.sexp` records the revised claims supported by the completed verification results.", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#427fe686df32"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 3, :text "**Status:** OPEN — IDENTIFY drafted 2026-05-07. MAP / DERIVE / ARGUE / VERIFY / INSTANTIATE / DOCUMENT to follow.", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#b619e42a0b9d"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 30, :text "The parent mission established a design recommendation for UKRN-S resting on a small computational simulation. That simulation has been useful as a stress-testing harness for the design's claims. But under the scrutiny it has now received — RNG-control audit, calibration against an empirically-grounded landscape, attempts to derive defensible parameter contrasts — the simulation has revealed that several of the working paper's load-bearing claims are not yet things the simulation can warrant.", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#f95e45fd6fa4"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 166, :text "6. The mission file's INSTANTIATE phase contains an explicit handoff: what UKRN-S' Researcher-Advisor role inherits when the WP's next iteration is run.", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#908a6e7abd6a"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 209, :text "- May 12, 2026 UKRN-S vision-day timing constraint: this mission does not need to be complete before that date, but its IDENTIFY framing should inform what is presented and what is held back as \"more research is needed\". (Today is May 7. This mission's IDENTIFY is the framing input for the away day.)", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#e3ba2836a149"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 377, :text "1. **Priority alignment.** UKRN-S' currently-active capabilities map onto the institution's strategic priorities (the Delta projection is positive).", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#91e133ab1e80"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 606, :text "- The UKRN-S abilities schema sketch (10 capabilities) and institutional abilities schema sketch (5 capabilities) are *sketches* — open to refinement during ARGUE and VERIFY. The structural shape is what's being committed to here, not the specific capability list.", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#6cbaf95f29b6"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 609, :text "- This DERIVE makes substantial commitments without yet writing code. The next phase (ARGUE) translates these architectural commitments into testable predictions — what we expect to see when the simulation runs and what would falsify the design's predictions. Then VERIFY runs the simulation.", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#94f588a314fc"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 620, :text "The ARGUE phase's job is to defend the v2 architecture against that risk by establishing its theoretical grounding. The grounding is *full active inference*: each architectural commitment in DERIVE maps onto, extends, or specialises an established AIF construct. The complexity is principled, not arbitrary — what we have built is what a faithful AIF simulation of the working paper's design *demands*, given the substrate the paper specifies.", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#f8e9532f9db0"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 622, :text "This frame also sets up VERIFY: the AIF formalism is operationalised (and uplift-able into futon5's AIF+ machinery) once the architecture is shown to be AIF-consistent. The VERIFY phase can then run the simulation as an active-inference agent rather than as a custom dynamical system whose theoretical status is uncertain.", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#f24b75219432"} {:kind :pending-lifecycle, :line 833, :text "*To be drafted. The INSTANTIATE phase will describe the handoff: how the new simulation enters the working paper's next iteration, who (Researcher-Advisor role) maintains it, and how it is updated when fresh evidence (T1 wave, indicators-track, additional reachability) arrives.*", :id "M-simulating-or-training-as-learning-system#cc9a4f5b24c3"}], :status-line "OPEN — IDENTIFY drafted 2026-05-07. MAP / DERIVE / ARGUE / VERIFY / INSTANTIATE / DOCUMENT to follow.", :operator-gate-lines []} {:path "/home/joe/code/futon6/holes/E-ground-G.md", :status-class :unknown, :source {:path "/home/joe/code/futon6/holes/E-ground-G.md", :sha256 "76b2d508136f8ad06a1a16fa593122b37086f1982c58861603dbe087f8ac5e3b"}, :title "Excursion: E-ground-G", :requisition {:absent :no-requisition}, :id "E-ground-G", :kind :excursion, :status-line "CHARTERED (IDENTIFY).", :mission-context {:parent "M-differentiable-substrate", :source {:path "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/TASK-CLASSIFICATION-LEDGER-2026-10-09.edn", :sha256 "ace9f837d69aee4af09e2a9ef621ac3e82b5c64d0a029ad67b573487dc9b1f2e"}}} {:path "/home/joe/code/futon1b/holes/E-SO-to-XT.md", :status-class :unknown, :source {:path "/home/joe/code/futon1b/holes/E-SO-to-XT.md", :sha256 "051dfb11050f8179dd6113e76cde653330cd0c494add65cbbdaf0c513e618170"}, :title "E-SO-to-XT — the StackExchange-family benchmark, from original contents", :requisition {:absent :no-requisition}, :id "E-SO-to-XT", :kind :excursion, :status-line nil, :mission-context {:parent "M-xtdb-22x-benchmarking", :source {:path "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/TASK-CLASSIFICATION-LEDGER-2026-10-09.edn", :sha256 "ace9f837d69aee4af09e2a9ef621ac3e82b5c64d0a029ad67b573487dc9b1f2e"}}} {:path "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/E-aif2-partB.md", :status-class :unknown, :source {:path "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/E-aif2-partB.md", :sha256 "2b92739ba7712a1725f9d8c1bf108b00951c6f844185cdd8382bae4ef41a66bb"}, :title "E-aif2-partB — can we trust the AIF specification? (a held deep-research excursion)", :requisition {:absent :no-requisition}, :id "E-aif2-partB", :kind :excursion, :status-line "**FIRST-PASS DONE (2026-06-24), full adversarial round still optional.** A first-pass triangula